<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    GApps product only: the MindTheGapps feed.

    This is the OTA half of "GApps builds are a first-class variant". v0.8.0 shipped
    as a GApps build (issues #11 and #14 were both filed against
    crDroidAndroid-...-a30s_gapps-v12.13.zip), but with the feed URL in the shared
    overlay every GApps device was polling a30s.json - the CLEAN feed. The Updater
    would offer a zip whose package list has no GmsCore/Phonesky/SetupWizard, and
    "Install" would replace a working GApps system with a clean one while looking
    like a routine OTA. Neither crDroid nor Lineage can express that in the app:
    UpdateChannel is RELEASE | TESTING (UserPreferencesRepository.kt:45) and a
    user-selectable "GApps channel" would be a footgun anyway, because switching a
    clean install to a GApps zip over OTA is not a supported transition - it is the
    same wrong direction in the other hat.

    So the feed follows the product. Product wiring:
    lineage_a30s_gapps.mk adds $(LOCAL_PATH)/overlay-lineage-gapps.

    The in-app Testing channel turns this into a30s_gapps_testing.json, which exists
    only if a GApps tester feed is ever published; a 404 there is the honest answer,
    not a silently wrong artifact.

    Feed: hm_mod/make_ota_json.py -channel gapps; asserted against the built APK by
    hm_mod/gate_ota_channel.sh.
-->
<resources>
    <string name="updater_server_url" translatable="false">https://raw.githubusercontent.com/HyperRamzey/device_samsung_a30s/ota/a30s_gapps.json</string>
</resources>
